Licence for packs/
==================

This directory holds law packs. Two different things live in every pack, and
they carry different licences.

1. The law text itself
----------------------

The text of a law, and any official translation of it, keeps the licence of the
official source it was taken from. That licence is declared in each pack's
pack.yaml, together with the source URL, the authoritative language and whether
a translation is official or unofficial.

Many jurisdictions exclude the text of laws from copyright altogether. Where
that is the case, the pack records the provision that says so. Nothing in this
file grants, restricts or alters any right in the law text: that is a matter
between you and the source.

Only the official source is authentic. A pack is a convenience for searching
and citing, not a substitute for the text published by the state.

2. The structural work around it
--------------------------------

Everything the project adds around the law text is licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International Licence (CC BY 4.0):

  - clause keys and the clause tree
  - breadcrumbs, cross-references and metadata
  - eval questions and starter questions
  - pack.yaml and any other file the project authors

Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Attribution: "DPOLens law packs (https://github.com/alkhatibdev/dpolens),
CC BY 4.0", with a note of any changes you made.

Code elsewhere in this repository is licensed under Apache-2.0. See ../LICENSE.
